  "id": "role-overload",
  "term": "role overload",
  "definition": "Role overload is a situation in which a person’s role places more demands on them than they can comfortably handle. In the source, it is described as a mixed stressor that can contribute to negative reactions such as withdrawal but can also prompt more active, adaptive responses such as job crafting.",
